{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired node1’s reservation utility for atomic, idempotent SQLite reservations on CentOS 5/Python 2.4. Existing data was preserved, concurrency and bounded lock behavior were verified, and the repair persisted across a confirmed node restart.","actions_performed":["Replaced unavailable sqlite3 module usage with the installed legacy sqlite module.","Added atomic BEGIN IMMEDIATE transactions with a five-second retry deadline.","Added positive-quantity validation, idempotent request replay, insufficient-stock rejection, and guarded stock decrements.","Verified competing requests cannot make stock negative and duplicate IDs decrement exactly once.","Restarted node1 once and confirmed its boot identity changed and the utility/database recovered.","Preserved CentOS 5.11, kernel 2.6.18-398.el5, stock=5, and reservation previous-request=2."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Compatible repaired utility","command_ids":["cmd-fc653ebd2714404d","cmd-2f961f2b7c294533"],"summary":"The repaired script compiles under Python 2.4 and retained the same checksum after restart."},{"requirement":"Preserve reservations, replay successful IDs, validate quantity, and reject insufficient stock","command_ids":["cmd-04d6ce3f301341c3"],"summary":"Replay returned the prior quantity without decrementing; zero and excessive quantities failed; production data remained unchanged."},{"requirement":"Competing requests keep remaining stock nonnegative","command_ids":["cmd-c6811aaa19c14498"],"summary":"Of two simultaneous quantity-4 requests against stock 5, one succeeded and one failed; remaining stock was 1 with zero negative rows."},{"requirement":"Successful request ID decrements exactly once","command_ids":["cmd-f9e8445450b0461d"],"summary":"Two simultaneous calls using the same ID both returned the same result, created one reservation row, and reduced stock from 5 to 3 once."},{"requirement":"Bounded lock waits","command_ids":["cmd-04ef0928575a4873"],"summary":"Under an independently held write lock, the request exited with code 75 after five seconds and made no database changes."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-a0115cebcaed459e","cmd-859f506793964e36","cmd-21be616ddf4a4926","cmd-2f961f2b7c294533"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 4244d945-3e4d-4348-8000-000000000000 was captured, restart was acknowledged, boot ID changed to dc6bec76-a7d4-4be4-8000-000000000000, and post-restart compilation, database integrity, persisted data, and live replay all passed."}]}
